From 9e3499039a775ed009f047fcb9d305a04e3a5932 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Lee <ethantlee21@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:35:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: ease the viewport move of a copy mode page motion
 under smooth-scroll

A half-page motion of copy mode moved the selection head, and
scrollToSelectionHead jumped the viewport with screen.scroll, which
records no distance. Helix scrolls its own region for the same key
(DECSTBM and SU), which the region scroll animation eases, so the two
looked different under smooth-scroll.

Now the head scroll records its move through rowScrollOffset, as a
wheel move does under smooth-scroll-rows, and flags the offset as a
move to ease (Screen.viewport_offset_eases). The renderer decays a
flagged offset in the plain smooth-scroll mode too. A wheel event, a
row-level scroll and a landed ease clear the flag, so a gesture
remainder is never decayed.
---
 .github/workflows/build-ghosttykit.yml |  2 +-
 src/Surface.zig                        | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++----
 src/renderer/generic.zig               | 26 +++++++++++++------
 src/terminal/Screen.zig                | 23 +++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 72 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

